Some thoughts while I grieve for my Valkyrie who died on level 19
while returning with the Amulet.... [Nethack 3.0 PL6]

Don't make the game much easier!  Yes, its hard, but it is winnable
and enjoyable (even though I haven't won yet).  I have *not* read
the sources, but I have availed myself of spoilers that have come
across the net.   Seems to be a reasonable compromise.  My Valkyrie
did rather well with only a modest amount of good fortune.

I suggest one slight help for the player though: make the wand of
probing work on objects (i.e. identify them).  Only allow the top
objects on a pile (1-3 random) to be identifed, per charge.

(minor spoilers discussed from here on)

I never found a wand of polymorph, so I never polymorphed a pile of
objects.  BTW, I agree that polymorphing's value should be lessened
by giving the polymorph a chance of destroying the object, and only 
a remote chance of producing a named weapon. 

Only found 3 very small shops, and no lawful altars (2 chaotic).

My piece of luck was finding a wizard's ghost that had a ring of conflict,
a magic marker, and a tinning kit.  Add that to the cloak of magic protection
and the Valkyrie's fighting capability and it was off to the races.

Now for the curious, some basic techniques of yours truly: 

	(Nethack 101 - apologies to veterans)

  1) Always keep a pet to check if things are cursed.  When a pet
     drops something next to you, reward it if you have a fresh
     corpse.  This behavior can be put to use to have the pet rob
     a shop.

  2) When quaffing unknown potions, try to go into a shop and pick
     up an unpaid item so the shopkeeper will block the door.  This
     will allow you to outwait nasty potions like paralysis and
     hallucination with a lower probability of being molested.  Of
     course you DID check that that potion wasn't cursed!  (A cursed
     potion of levitation will send you through the roof, with a
     level of Kops to get through below now.)

  3) When reading scrolls, drop all potions and scrolls until the
     scroll of fire has been found -- or use a bag to protect them.
     If you have a scare monster scroll, don't drop it, put it in
     a chest.  If you haven't discovered the destroy armor scroll,
     take off anything good, and wear a cheaper piece before reading.
     Lastly, don't read those spellbooks until you find the scroll
     of amnesia.

  4) On trying wands: make sure that the monster you try an unknown
     wand on moves at the same speed you do.  You will be able to
     see if the wand was a speed or slow monster wand.  Either one
     is a great find (zap speed monster on yourself!). Make sure
     there's plenty of open space behind the monster (bouncing a
     wand of death can ruin your whole day).  If nothing seems to
     happen to the monster, try zapping the wand at a corpse
     (undead turning will revive the corpse), then at locked/unlocked
     doors (wands of locking/unlocking).

  5) Don't throw that wand of make invisible away! Use it to zap
     floating eyes, to kill them safely.

  6) Dungeon chemistry can be fun!  Don't discard weak or harmful potions,
     #dip one into another.  Oftentimes you'll lose both, but frequently
     the mixture will clear into water.  Drop the water on lawful
     altars to make holy water.  Unholy water also has its uses, as
     cursed scrolls of teleporation (level teleport) become useful late
     in the game.  If you have two or more water potions that will
     group, you can #dip them into a holy water potion for a net increase
     in holy water.  I've noticed that created water normally won't
     group - in this case I will #dip one unknown created water into
     another until I get that satisfying aura.

  7) That tinning kit is very useful! Often in the heat of battle, you
     would not be able to eat a useful corpse (e.g. a wraith) uninter-
     rupted.  So tin it!  Tinning dead dragons reduces bloating. And
     tinning a dead troll prevents it from rising from the dead.
     BTW, I tinned the Wizard of Yendor after the first time I killed
     him, but the sucker still came back to haunt me later.  Yes, I
     did die with a tin of Wizard of Yendor meat.

  8) Don't waste holy water taking curses off. #dip cursed items into
     fountains, but engrave Elbereth before you #dip in case of snakes, etc.
	 Also use fountains to change useless scrolls into blank scrolls
     (love that magic marker!).


Now some notes on how the Valkyrie got so far:
(Major Spoilers contained below)

   Once I found the dead wizard's cache, I grabbed the good stuff, and
   ran upstairs to every fountain it took until I had the curses off the
   cloak, ring of conflict, and the magic marker.  Dungeon chemistry
   had given me plenty of holy water, so I wrote three enchant weapon
   scrolls (I had already discovered it, so my long sword was +2),
   and I enchanted two of them.  Now, I had no booze, but it wasn't 
   long before some rotten food  confused me. PRESTO! read the normal
   enchant weapon scroll and the sword was now rustproof.  Now it was
   time to run around and #dip the sword (since it can't rust) until
   it became Excalibur.

   My second piece of fortune occurred here: In the process of making
   Excalibur, I unleashed a grateful water demon and scored a set of
   speed boots.  Once the lady did her thing, I read the two blessed
   enchant weapon scrolls, and had a +8 Excalibur.  This kicks butt!
   (I have never had Mjollnir, but I did get Stormbringer later in
   the game - I tried it for a while but +8 Excalibur is much better).

   For the next few hours, the dungeon ran with blood.  Got down to the
   castle level without an instrument or a ring of levitation.  That's
   OK, you can tunnel along the outer wall to the back and fall into a
   trap door just inside the back door.  Later on, in hell, I did get
   a levitation ring, so I went back up and cleaned out the castle to
   get the wand of wishing to get a ring of teleport control...

   Found the Wiz with a binary search using level teleporters. Oh yeah,
   I always put a blindfold on prior to entering a new level (especially
   before Medusa has been found!).  So its easy to see when you hit the
   Wiz - plus the blindfold/mirror trick tells you whether he's above
   or below.  Killed him after a moderate battle - he tried "Touch of
   Death" 3 times, but it didn't work.  I'm not sure if that's because
   of the black dragon I ate or what.  Then I tinned him.

   So how did my Valkyrie croak?  Turns out once you have the amulet,
   the gods begin to S--t on you.  I had never carried much food, relying
   on prayer.  I couldn't level teleport anymore, so I began trudging
   out of the dungeon, with my inventory slowing becoming cursed.  The
   Wiz resurrected himself once, and was a minor nuisance.  Even though
   the gods were dumping on me, Loki stuck by me and fed me for a while.
   Once he turned on me though, I was finished.  Ran out of comestibles
   and couldn't kill new food fast enough.  Starting fainting on level 19
   and a lowly ice troll did me in.  Arrrghh!

   So what did I learn?  Next time, before I clobber the Wiz, I'll put all
   the gold and jewels (I was dragging quite a hoard) up on level one.
   Then I'll leave tins of food on every other level to make sure I don't
   starve on the way out.


Some final observations:

   Nymphs aren't too much trouble when you have boots of speed, but they
   have ruined other fine games for me.  My blessed scrolls of genocide
   are saved for Nymphs.  I normally use an unblessed scroll of genocide
   to wipe out Rust Monsters.

   Prudence dictates keeping a lizard corpse on hand to deal with the
   occasional "stoning" hit from a cockatrice.

   Careful monitoring of rec.games.hack (esp. postings from David Hairston)
   makes one a better player.
